Body:
Ok, in my case, I've fixed it in the configuration by allowing the skills. E.g. in opencode config file:

```
...
  "permission": {
    "skill": {
      "*": "allow"
    }
  }
...
```

or set it in `OPENCODE_PERMISSION` variable (see [schema](https://opencode.ai/config.json)).

> how are u hooking it up in opencode? Im assuming you arent setting it up correctly, recommend using the anthropic compat setup if you find it works well in claude code, dont use openai compatible unless you know what fields / settings to set

I'm not sure if it's openai or anthropic . Here is what I see in ~/.config/opencode.json :

```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "my-local": {
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "http://higgs.localdomain:8001/v1",
        "apiKey": "sk-dummy"
      },
      "models": {
        "qwen-3.6": {
          "id": "qwen-3.6",
          "options": {
            "thinking": false
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

When I use claude code, here is how I set it up :

```
export ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL="http://higgs.localdomain:8001"
export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY='sk-no-key-required' ## or 'sk-1234'
```
